    "body": "Set up an analytics platform so we can learn about which questions get clicks and start A/B testing.\r\n\r\nDesired features:\r\n1. Exclude EU for GDPR reasons (we don't want to have cookie notices)\r\n2. Ability to watch recorded user sessions (does not need to be a huge number)\r\n3. Collect statistics on how many times any given question is displayed and how many times it is clicked and opened (and the ratio between them) - also used for initial questions\r\n4. Collect statistics on the last question a user clicks before leaving\r\n5. Ability to run A/B tests on general site features (e.g. intro line)\r\n6. Statistics on average time on site, answers opened count, links clicked, etc\r\n7. Logging each search in the search bar (but cutting the half-typed ones when immediately followed by an extended string)\r\n8. Stats on what people clicked before clicking to a specific question (e.g. \"I'm convinced, how can I help?\")\r\n\r\n\r\nPerhaps one of these would work\r\nhttps://livesession.io/ \r\nhttps://logrocket.com/\r\nhttps://www.smartlook.com/\r\nhttps://mouseflow.com/\r\nhttps://www.inspectlet.com/\r\nhttps://watchthem.live/\r\nhttps://www.hotjar.com/\r\n\r\nOr something else.",
